                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "This week, I led a letter with my Maryland colleagues urging GOP leaders to reopen the government, prevent skyrocketing health care costs, and protect rural health care access. Without action, premiums will spike for thousands of Marylanders\u2013including 21,000 people in the 6th District alone. Moreover, rural hospitals, clinics, and mental health and addiction facilities across the state are at risk of closing or reducing essential services. We must act. \n\nRead the letter: https://t.co/6QrL2jDc0H",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1760732407,
                "view_count": 183
            },
            {
